# Otharri, Suns' Glory is cast on turn 9 and attacks the same turn, because he has haste. His trigger gives Bot1 an
# experience counter and then makes one 2/2 red Rebel per experience counter (CR 122.1, 508.4) — so the first attack
# makes one Rebel, tapped and attacking, and it was never declared. Lifelink on a 3/3 flier takes Bot2 to 15 and puts
# Bot1 to 23, and the Rebel adds 2 more.
#
# Turn 11 is the half a single attack cannot show: a second counter, and now two Rebels at once rather than one,
# because the count is the player's running total and not anything on the creature. Otharri dying and buying himself
# back out of the graveyard is the other half, and it is in CubeOtharriTests, which can kill him on purpose.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Plains
Plains
Otharri, Suns' Glory
Mountain x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T9 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Otharri, Suns' Glory.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

# Haste: he attacks the turn he arrives. The counter comes before the count, so one Rebel, not none.
Bot1.Attack(Otharri, Suns' Glory > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Experience = 1
? Combat.Attackers = Otharri, Suns' Glory > Bot2; Rebel Token > Bot2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Rebel Token.Tapped = True
[T9 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 15
? Bot1.Life = 23

[T11 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Otharri, Suns' Glory > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Experience = 2
[T11 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 11
Bot1.Experience = 2
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Mountain; Mountain; Plains; Plains; Otharri, Suns' Glory; Rebel Token; Rebel Token; Rebel Token
